WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.540
Maryland’s Section 15-418 applies to certain plans that offer dependent coverage.

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:09.080
It includes unmarried child dependents under 25, including the insured’s grandchild

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:13.620
or a child eligible under the state’s separate dependent coverage law.

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:18.986
They receive the same benefits at the same premium as other covered dependents.

00:00:18.986 --> 00:00:21.050
The federal rule is different.

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:25.590
When a plan covers a parent’s children, they can generally stay

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:29.717
enrolled until age 26, regardless of marital or student status.

00:00:29.717 --> 00:00:35.495
On the exam, check whether the question asks about a child or a grandchild.

00:00:35.495 --> 00:00:39.210
Maryland’s section excludes accident-only, disability and long-term care coverage.

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:44.501
Section 15-401 makes a newborn covered from the moment of birth and an adopted

00:00:44.501 --> 00:00:49.792
child covered from the date of adoption, defined as the earlier of the judicial

00:00:49.792 --> 00:00:55.082
decree or the assumption of custody pending adoption; a minor placed under a court

00:00:55.082 --> 00:00:59.995
or testamentary guardianship of at least twelve months is covered from the appointment.

00:00:59.995 --> 00:01:03.396
Coverage includes care for congenital defects and birth abnormalities.

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:07.553
If the policy charges a premium for the child, the insurer

00:01:07.553 --> 00:01:11.711
may require notice and payment within 31 days after the birth,

00:01:11.711 --> 00:01:15.490
adoption or appointment to continue coverage beyond those 31 days.

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:19.269
Insurers must offer family coverage on request regardless of marital

00:01:19.269 --> 00:01:22.670
status and must disclose when it is not included.

00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:27.455
Under Section 15-405, when a parent is ordered to provide health coverage for

00:01:27.455 --> 00:01:32.239
a child, the carrier must enroll the child regardless of enrollment periods, at

00:01:32.239 --> 00:01:37.024
the request of either parent, the child support agency or the Department of

00:01:37.024 --> 00:01:41.809
Health, and may not refuse because the child was born outside marriage, is

00:01:41.809 --> 00:01:45.121
not a tax dependent, lives elsewhere or receives Medicaid.

00:01:45.121 --> 00:01:49.170
Carriers act on a medical support notice within 20 business days.

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:53.586
Separately, a dependent child who reaches the limiting age but cannot support

00:01:53.586 --> 00:01:58.003
himself because of an intellectual disability or physical handicap, and who depends

00:01:58.003 --> 00:02:02.419
on the insured, stays covered as long as the incapacity continues, with

00:02:02.419 --> 00:02:06.100
proof furnished when the age is reached and periodically thereafter.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:10.083
A mandated offer requires the insurer to make a

00:02:10.083 --> 00:02:14.066
benefit available; the policyholder chooses whether to buy it.

00:02:14.066 --> 00:02:19.820
Section 15-801 is the model: insurers and nonprofit health service plans issuing group

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:25.573
policies on an expense-incurred basis must offer the policyholder the option of benefits

00:02:25.573 --> 00:02:31.326
for the care of people with Alzheimer’s disease, including nursing home and custodial

00:02:31.326 --> 00:02:37.080
care, and a similar option for elderly people with other diseases the Commissioner

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:41.505
designates, subject to reasonable limits such as copayments and maximums.

00:02:41.505 --> 00:02:45.488
Priya may accept or decline the option for her

00:02:45.488 --> 00:02:49.472
bakery; the carrier may not fail to offer it.

00:02:49.472 --> 00:02:53.012
Continuation rights after death, divorce and job loss

00:02:53.012 --> 00:02:56.110
are also required features of group contracts.

00:02:56.110 --> 00:03:00.644
A mandated benefit must be included in the policy.

00:03:00.644 --> 00:03:04.673
Maryland’s list is long; the exam favors these.

00:03:04.673 --> 00:03:10.718
Mental health and substance use disorder treatment at parity with physical illness,

00:03:10.718 --> 00:03:16.259
including partial hospitalization for at least 60 days, under Section 15-802.

00:03:16.259 --> 00:03:20.793
Off-label drug uses recognized in standard references, Section 15-804.

00:03:20.793 --> 00:03:27.845
In vitro fertilization for policies with pregnancy benefits, up to three attempts per live

00:03:27.845 --> 00:03:34.897
birth and a 100,000 dollar lifetime limit, with a religious organization exception, Section 15-810.

00:03:34.897 --> 00:03:37.416
Reconstructive breast surgery after mastectomy.

00:03:37.416 --> 00:03:43.964
Hearing aids for minors, 1,400 dollars per ear every 36 months, Section 15-838.

00:03:43.964 --> 00:03:48.498
Surgery for morbid obesity meeting NIH standards, Section 15-839.

00:03:48.498 --> 00:03:55.550
Tobacco cessation drugs and two 90-day courses of nicotine replacement a year, Section 15-841.

00:03:55.550 --> 00:03:58.066
Several Maryland rules complete the picture.

00:03:58.066 --> 00:04:02.258
Carriers must pay or respond to claims within 30 days,

00:04:02.258 --> 00:04:06.032
with interest on late clean claims, under Section 15-1005.

00:04:06.032 --> 00:04:09.386
Members may grieve adverse decisions and complain to

00:04:09.386 --> 00:04:12.321
the Administration, which can order independent review.

00:04:12.321 --> 00:04:17.352
A certificate holder whose spouse dies may add the children who were

00:04:17.352 --> 00:04:21.964
on the spouse’s policy within six months without evidence of insurability.

00:04:21.964 --> 00:04:27.414
Mandated benefits and offers bind insurers, nonprofit health service plans and HMOs alike.

00:04:27.414 --> 00:04:31.607
The Maryland Health Care Commission evaluates the cost of mandates.

00:04:31.607 --> 00:04:36.638
When a question names a Maryland requirement, ask three things: who must

00:04:36.638 --> 00:04:41.250
comply, who is covered and what must be offered or paid.
